{"metadata":{"title":"Using Imported C Structs and Unions in Swift","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Standard Library"}]},"kind":"article","sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Language-interoperability","title":"Language interoperability","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/c-interoperability","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/cxx-interoperability","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/customizing-your-c-code-for-swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-macros-in-swift"],"generated":true}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how Swift represents imported C structures and unions, including types with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bitfields and unnamed fields."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift imports any C structure declared in a C header as a Swift structure. The imported"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Swift structure contains a stored property for each C structure field and an initializer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose parameters correspond to the stored properties."}]},{"text":"Structures with Default Values","anchor":"Structures-with-Default-Values","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If all imported members have default values, Swift also provides a default initializer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that takes no arguments. For example, given the following C structure:"}]},{"syntax":"occ","code":["struct Color {","    float r, g, b;","};","typedef struct Color Color;"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When you import the Color structure, the Swift version is equivalent to the following:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public struct Color {","    var r: Float","    var g: Float","    var b: Float","","    init()","    init(r: Float, g: Float, b: Float)","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Unions","level":3,"text":"Unions"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swift imports C unions as Swift structures. Although Swift doesn’t support natively","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declared unions, a C union imported as a Swift structure still behaves like a C union.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"For example, consider a C union named ","type":"text"},{"code":"SchroedingersCat","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that has an ","type":"text"},{"code":"isAlive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"code":"isDead","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" field:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["union SchroedingersCat {","    bool isAlive;","    bool isDead;","};"],"syntax":"occ","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In Swift, it’s imported like this:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct SchroedingersCat {","    var isAlive: Bool { get set }","    var isDead: Bool { get set }","","    init(isAlive: Bool)","    init(isDead: Bool)","","    init()","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Because unions in C use the same base memory address for all of their fields, all","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the computed properties in a union imported by Swift use the same underlying memory.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"As a result, changing the value of a property on an instance of the imported structure","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"changes the value of all other properties defined by that structure.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In the example below, changing the value of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"isAlive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" computed property on an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instance of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SchroedingersCat","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" structure also changes the value of the instance’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"isDead","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" computed property:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var mittens = SchroedingersCat(isAlive: false)","","print(mittens.isAlive, mittens.isDead)","\/\/ Prints \"false false\"","","mittens.isAlive = true","print(mittens.isDead)","\/\/ Prints \"true\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"text":"Bit Fields","anchor":"Bit-Fields","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift imports bit fields that are declared in structures, like those found in Foundation’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSDecimal"},{"type":"text","text":" type, as computed properties. When accessing a computed property corresponding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to a bit field, Swift automatically converts the value to and from compatible Swift"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"types."}]},{"text":"Unnamed Structure and Union Fields","anchor":"Unnamed-Structure-and-Union-Fields","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"C "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"struct"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"union"},{"type":"text","text":" types can define fields that have no name or that are of an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unnamed type. Unnamed fields consist of a nested "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"struct"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"union"},{"type":"text","text":" type with named"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fields."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For example, consider a C structure named "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Cake"},{"type":"text","text":" that contains the fields "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"layers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"height"},{"type":"text","text":" nested within an unnamed union type, and a field "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"toppings"},{"type":"text","text":" of an unnamed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"struct type:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["struct Cake {","    union {","        int layers;","        double height;","    };","","    struct {","        bool icing;","        bool sprinkles;","    } toppings;","};"],"syntax":"occ"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Cake"},{"type":"text","text":" structure has been imported, you can use the default initializer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to create an instance and use it as follows:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var simpleCake = Cake()","simpleCake.layers = 5","print(simpleCake.toppings.icing)","\/\/ Prints \"false\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The imported "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Cake"},{"type":"text","text":" structure and its nested types are imported with a memberwise"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"initializer that you can use to initialize the structure with custom values for its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fields:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let cake = Cake(","    .init(layers: 2),","    toppings: .init(icing: true, sprinkles: false)",")","","print(\"The cake has \\(cake.layers) layers.\")","\/\/ Prints \"The cake has 2 layers.\"","print(\"Does it have sprinkles?\", cake.toppings.sprinkles ? \"Yes.\" : \"No.\")","\/\/ Prints \"Does it have sprinkles? No.\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because the first field of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Cake"},{"type":"text","text":" structure is unnamed, its initializer’s first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parameter doesn’t have a label. Because the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Cake"},{"type":"text","text":" structure has fields with unnamed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"types, you use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".init"},{"type":"text","text":" initializers (allowed due to Swift’s type inference) to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set the initial value for each of the structure’s unnamed fields."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift"]]},"references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","role":"collection","title":"Standard Library","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Standard Library","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swift","abstract":[{"text":"Browse the essential types provided by Swift’s standard library.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/using-imported-c-macros-in-swift":{"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/using-imported-c-macros-in-swift","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-macros-in-swift","title":"Using Imported C Macros in Swift","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Use imported C-defined macros as constants.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/customizing-your-c-code-for-swift":{"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/customizing-your-c-code-for-swift","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/customizing-your-c-code-for-swift","title":"Customizing Your C Code for Swift","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Use the ","type":"text"},{"code":"CF_SWIFT_NAME","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro to group functions that have related behavior.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/cxx-interoperability":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/cxx-interoperability","title":"C++ Interoperability","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/cxx-interoperability","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[{"text":"Work with standard C++ types.","type":"text"}]},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/c-interoperability":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Use imported C types or call C variadic functions."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/c-interoperability","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","title":"C Interoperability","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/c-interoperability"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift","title":"Using Imported C Functions in Swift","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how to call imported functions that are declared in a C header."}]}}}